## Why This Is Asked
Tests experience designing scalable, governed data platforms with multi-tenant isolation, data contracts, and end-to-end lineage on GCP. It also probes handling late-arriving data, PII masking, and per-tenant rollback plans.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant isolation in BigQuery with Authorized Views
- Data contracts and lineage via Data Catalog
- Ingestion-time PII masking with DLP
- Event-time processing and late-arrivals in Dataflow
- Cross-region replication and immutable audit logs
- Schema evolution and per-tenant rollback strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: ingest path with DLP masking before storage
const ingest = (record) => {
  const masked = dlp.maskPII(record);
  pubsub.publish(masked);
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test schema evolution across 300 tenants without downtime?
- What metrics and alerting would you implement for cross-region replication health?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical observability and data reliability skills in a real-world, beginner-friendly setting.

## Key Concepts
- Beam Metrics and Cloud Monitoring integration
- Idempotent streaming writes with insertId
- Lightweight auditing and error handling
- Alerting on data quality metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-beam sketch (JavaScript/TypeScript syntax used for illustration)
class ParseEvent extends DoFn {
  @ProcessElement
  process(@Element json, output) {
    const event = JSON.parse(json.image);
    this.ingested.inc();
    // ... validation and transformation
    this.processed.inc();
    output(event);
  }

  @Setup
  setup() {
    this.ingested = Metrics.counter('pipeline', 'ingested_events');
    this.processed = Metrics.counter('pipeline', 'processed_events');
    this.failed = Metrics.counter('pipeline', 'failed_events');
  }
}
```

